<title>GERMANY: Stark says no plan to make 2, 5-yr debt strippable.</title>
<headline>Stark says no plan to make 2, 5-yr debt strippable.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Juergen Stark, state secretary in the German finance ministry, said on Tuesday that the government did not intend to make its two- and five-year bonds strippable.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no intention to make two- or five-year paper strippable,&quot; Stark said at the news conference called to announce the issue of a new strippable 30-year bond.</p>
<p>Stark earlier told the news conference that Bonn intended to issue more strippable bonds and said the government was keen to ensure the full range of the yield curve was covered with German debt issues.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
